#heading(level: 2, "Interpretation and next hypothesis")
#text("Generic polynomial/provenance axpy, exponent-vector construction and allocator functions appear in the recorded self hotspots. The visible allocator category counts only six named allocator/wrapper symbols present in the top25; it is a lower bound, not the whole allocation cost. Self instruction categories are separate from overlapping inclusive call paths. Instruction share does not measure elapsed-time share, cache latency or cycles.")
#parbreak()
#text("The profile covers the child, including construction/internal checks, wire serialization, first complete replay and proof writes. Controller readback/second replay, process launch and wrappers remain in the agreed application-call measurement boundary but are outside child instruction attribution. Profile wall durations are excluded from all performance statistics. The earlier repeated full-boundary96 result is unchanged; no improvement is admitted. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("The next hypothesis is a complete packed polynomial/provenance representation through construction, with guarded exact field arithmetic, rather than storing only two extra local resultant nodes. HYPOTHESIS_PACKED_PIPELINE_182.md defines the candidate and its required controls. It is a proposed implementation, not a guaranteed15x route. Transport/serialization changes must be applied to matched controls too, and full-boundary measurement remains decisive. [pcc:unverified]")
